Subject: [PATCH] turnip: linear and modifier external images need no dedicated allocation

Every externally-imported image reported requiresDedicatedAllocation, so a
Vulkan client importing host pages or dma-bufs at a pitch the driver's own
layout already matches (Metal's IOSurfaces: 1125-wide BGRA at 4608 bytes is
exactly fd6's align(4500, 256)) could not bind its image at an offset of that
import, and fell back to per-use shadow copies of the whole surface: 1,460
shadowed textures and 108,922 copies in one 90-second desktop session.

Linear and DRM-modifier layouts are fixed-pitch: they bind at any offset the
image's alignment allows inside the import, so only tiled external images
keep the dedicated requirement.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -1169,8 +1169,15 @@
       case VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_MEMORY_DEDICATED_REQUIREMENTS: {
          VkMemoryDedicatedRequirements *req =
             (VkMemoryDedicatedRequirements *) ext;
+         /* Linear and DRM-modifier images are laid out at fixed pitches and
+          * bind at any offset their alignment allows inside an imported
+          * allocation; only tiled external images (AHB's compressed layouts)
+          * need the allocation to themselves.
+          */
          req->requiresDedicatedAllocation =
-            image->vk.external_handle_types != 0;
+            image->vk.external_handle_types != 0 &&
+            image->vk.tiling != VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR &&
+            image->vk.tiling != VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT;
          req->prefersDedicatedAllocation = req->requiresDedicatedAllocation;
          break;
       }
